  "description": "Built-in canonical marker sets for the major cell types of human tissue (and of mouse, by case-insensitive symbol matching). Every gene of a set is listed as a human marker of the PanglaoDB cell type(s) named in the set's 'panglaodb' field (PanglaoDB marker table of 27 March 2020 as redistributed by OmniPath; Franzen, Gan and Bjorkegren 2019, Database baz046, doi:10.1093/database/baz046), checked with scripts/verify_builtin_markers.py. Genes were chosen from those markers by hand: well-established, specific (low PanglaoDB ubiquitousness), 3-7 per set, so that a targeted imaging panel of a few hundred genes still holds two or more for the main compartments. Only the genes present in the panel are scored; a set with fewer than MIN_GENES_PRESENT present genes is skipped. Symbols are HGNC.",
